title Caravan confer -- the reach itself travels, rather than riding along from the spawn
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the road-ahead itineraries; Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; council rota one doc; send each finished increment
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md whole -- rows 80, 83, 84, 85 each read closed, and the prose notes below them likewise. Row 85 was closed for real on 20260819.134229 with 129 fragile sites converted and seven witnesses re-run on metal, so the apostrophe loom is a check now rather than a habit. Nothing agent-closable stood open, and the line was clear for constructive work.
think Council rota by lap index: 484 .kyri logs on disk when the lap opened, so lap 485, and 485 mod 27 = 26 -- the 1,024-round itinerary. Read it beside item 25, the eight-season double-seat, since the prompt names both as road-ahead reading. The Lindy-priority Microkernel Target double-seat sits ahead of Seasons A-H, and this Caravan arc is exactly that double-seat's agent-doable spine.
think The running thread was unambiguous and had been named three laps running. entrust.rye closed by naming the one thing it could not reach, in its module prose, its README section, and its witness header alike: a child was spawned holding capability words for its whole reserve, so what grew when the run entrusted an arc was the run's PERMISSION, never the child's REACH. This lap binds that.
think The first design question was whether the gap is real or merely aesthetic, and the tree answered it directly. serve.reach_by_name refuses a region a child's capability list does not name, with error.NotGranted. So a child spawned narrowed to its line alone genuinely cannot touch a reserve arc -- the isolation is physical rather than promised. That made the rung provable rather than decorative before a line of it was written.
think The second question was what carries the word. entrust already published a count over a note and heard an answer back; this rung publishes the WORDS themselves beside that count, in the same region:perm grammar the spawn argv already speaks, one word per line. The words land first and the count that makes them live lands second, so a child reading between the two writes sees fewer words than exist rather than a count naming a word that has not arrived.
think The third question was where the word comes from, and the answer is the whole safety of the act: derived, never authored. The run reads the domain's ceiling out of the table roster.from_system derives from the declaration, masks it to the letter the reserve declares, renders it, and reads its own rendering back before publishing. A supervisor cannot invent a right the document withholds, because it never writes a mask -- it copies one and proves the copy.
think The fourth question was how a child knows when to stop waiting. Under the elder reach it could derive its reserve from its own slot; under this one it holds nothing beyond its line, so it cannot. Added an .offered note seated before the spawn -- a promise about the future rather than a capability -- so the child waits exactly as long as there is reach still coming and comes home the moment the last word is grafted.
think The fifth question was what number the two rooms disagree on, since this rung buys neither speed nor room. Named it DARK REACH: arcs a running child could physically touch that the door has not yet weighed. Handing every word at the spawn leaves it above zero; conferring drives it to zero with the same children carrying the same work home. The child measures it in its own hands by asking for each arc before grafting its word, so the finding is reported by the party that would be lying if it were false.
obs The two rooms disagree on isolation alone, and that is the honest shape of this rung rather than a weakness. taper bought more children at once, entrust bought fewer children for the same work, and confer buys neither -- 3 children and 1 carried home under both reaches, with dark reach falling from 1 to 0. A rung that improved a throughput number here would have been measuring the wrong thing; the claim this arc has been making about isolation is what was owed a witness.
obs The child's own report is the strongest line in the run: read 3 arcs of its own, 1 conferred, 1 reachable before the word arrived under the elder reach, and the identical line ending in 0 under this one. Same binary, same plan, same declaration; only when the word arrives differs.
obs All six RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN was claimed. Drop the region refusal and a word travels for a region the document never granted. Drop the letter refusal and a word carries a write the ceiling withholds. Drop the wire round-trip and a right outside the three-word grammar renders anyway as something narrower. Widen the room bound and a word travels to a child with no room to hold it. Publish a count of nothing and the run refuses the whole record with ConferUnheld rather than believing reach grafted that never was. Let the child skip the graft and it answers NotGranted on the conferred arc while carrying fine when every word rode along from the spawn -- the whole rung, read from the child's side.
obs The compiler caught the fourth RED path before the runtime could. Removing the ConferOverfull bound outright made write_words' line_arcs parameter unused, which Rye refuses to compile -- an honest refusal, and a reminder that a guard whose only purpose is a parameter is structurally load-bearing. Widened the bound instead, and the fixture then failed exactly as intended.
obs The ConferGarbled path needed a fixture the declaration could not supply, and finding it taught something worth keeping. The wire carries three permission words -- r, rw, rx -- so a ceiling holding right_net renders as plain r and reads back narrower than it was. Built a hand-seated table with that grant to prove the round-trip refusal fires. The lesson generalizes: any right the capability table can hold and the wire cannot spell must refuse rather than quietly shrink.
obs Docs stayed synced in the same round, as the ratchet the last two laps opened asks. entrust's README limit paragraph said carrying a capability into a running child belonged to the vision room until a witness binds it; a witness now binds it, so that paragraph points at Confer, and the module table gained its row in the same edit rather than drifting behind.
loom witness=caravan_confer_witness result=GREEN phases=4 children_at_spawn=3 children_on_grant=3 homed=1 conferred=1 dark_at_spawn=1 dark_on_grant=0 pairs_agreed=9 red_paths_proven=6
file caravan/confer.rye the reach itself travels -- the derived word, the bounded wire, five refusals, and the child that grafts before it reads
file tools/caravan_confer_witness.rish the witness on metal, reading every claim natively and naming all six proven RED paths
file caravan/README.md the Confer section, the module table row, and entrust's limit line repointed now that a witness binds it
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moved to this rung, the entrust edge condensed to a pointer
recommend keep-going the next rung's question is already named and is this rung's own mirror: whether a supervisor may REVOKE a capability from a child already running, deleting reach mid-flight as a real microkernel deletes a cspace slot. A conferred word grows a child's list and never prunes it, so revocation is the one direction the wire has not carried. Mechanical, single-module, and the arc's habit answers how to shape it -- the hard half will be that a revocation must be refused wherever the child is mid-read, which a grant never had to check. The caravan witness loom -- 50 per-rung witnesses and no choir that hears them all -- stands beside it as an equally honest keystone, and has now been named as a ratchet three times.
